ADR Identification Report

Patient: Female, 45 years
Diagnosis: Mucinous cystadenoma of ovary
Suspected drug: Augmentin 625 mg
Generic: Amoxicillin + Clavulanic acid
Suspected ADR: White vaginal discharge

1. Description of ADR

The patient developed white vaginal discharge during the treatment period. Augmentin contains a broad-spectrum antibiotic combination that can disturb the normal vaginal flora and may predispose to Candida overgrowth, resulting in vulvovaginal candidiasis.

2. Suspected Drug

Augmentin (Amoxicillin + Clavulanic acid)

3. Possible Mechanism

Broad-spectrum antibiotics can suppress normal protective bacterial flora. This alteration of the vaginal microbiota may allow Candida species to proliferate, potentially causing vulvovaginal candidiasis and white vaginal discharge.

4.Relationship between drug and the adverse effect 

The treatment chart documents Augmentin administration during the patient's hospital stay, and white vaginal discharge was subsequently documented. This provides a temporal association between drug exposure and the suspected reaction.
